From 5425ccdeea469dd5fa4c90b307d329074fb02bd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:11:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cuda: RDNA4 decode/prefill kernel speedups: qwen4exp
 hc_mix + IQ2/IQ3/K-quant paths (bit-exact)

qwen4exp only (GGML_OP_HC_MIX):
- band up kernel (all tokens per block, reduction only over the warp's own rows), also for nt=1
- v = silu(lo/hc) quantized once in the down_dots tail (per-(token, group) counters)
- rms_gamma_quant keeps x/xn in registers

General (any model using these types/shapes):
- mmvq: 2 rows per block for 1-token dense decode on RDNA4 (GGML_MMVQ_RDNA4_WEIGHT_RPB1)
- mmvq: IQ2_XS MoE item-loop unroll 2
- mmvf: F32 K-loop unroll 4; one cross-warp exchange for all columns at nt > 1
- vecdotq/mmq loaders: cheaper IQ2_XXS/IQ2_XS/IQ3_XXS sign application (apply_ksigns)
- mmq (AMD MMA path): unroll 1 in the q8_0_16 and q8_1 vec dots (J=16 / J<=64 spilled on gfx12)
- mmq: IQ2_XS/IQ3_XXS take the RDNA3.5/RDNA4 routed-compact MoE path
- test-backend-ops: HC_MIX cases, Flash-Next matmul perf shapes, 512-expert TOPK_MOE case

Every output keeps its accumulation order; byte-identical to the unpatched build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
